  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-59838",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "In the model, there are $2$ shapes. Each shape consists of $3$ pieces that each represent $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a whole. There are $6$ pieces in total.\n\nThe model tells us that when we divide $2$ wholes into thirds, we will be left with $6$ pieces.\n\nHence, the division problem is:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\,2\\,}÷\\frac{1}{3}=\\boxed{\\,6\\,}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing numbers are $2$ and $6.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
